    Two-phase exactness fully characterized; n<=22 hit/miss table; tau(n)=Omega(n) drift
    
    Proved (paper proof): optimal strict two-phase worst case is exactly
    S(n-1)+ceil(log2 n) and is exact-budget iff S(n)=S(n-1)+ceil(log2 n)
    (threshold-realizable height-ceil(log2 n) gap tree in phase 2). Combined
    with the known exact values through n=22 (Wells, Peczarski, Stober-Weiss;
    OEIS A036604): two-phase exact at n in {4,6,7,8,11,12,13,14,15,16,22},
    misses at {5,9,10,17,18,19,20,21}; non-monotone (five consecutive misses
    17-21, then a hit at 22). Independent execution witness at n=9 recorded.
    Deduction: the cumulative miss mass tau(n)=T(n)-S(n) satisfies
    tau(n) >= n/4 - O(n/(log n)^(1/5)) = Omega(n) (elementary dyadic-block
    count + Sergeev).

